const sections = [
  {title:'Not all screen time serves the same purpose', paragraphs:[
    'A child watching an endless stream of suggested videos and a child following a picture-based bedtime routine may both be using a screen, but the experiences are fundamentally different. The meaningful question is not only how long a screen is used; it is what that screen is helping a child practice.',
    'Goally is built around deliberate activities: early learning, guided routines, communication and daily skills. Entertainment still has a place in childhood. But a dedicated learning device can make purposeful use the default rather than something parents must assemble from an enormous app store.'
  ]},
  {title:'Visual schedules can make independence feel achievable', paragraphs:[
    'Getting dressed, brushing teeth, eating breakfast and packing a bag are familiar tasks for adults. For young children, the sequence can be difficult to remember or overwhelming to begin. Goally lets parents build visual routines with photos, audio prompts and step-by-step tasks.',
    'Instead of repeating a long list of instructions, caregivers can show what comes next. Completing one manageable step at a time gives children opportunities to practice following through. Progress will vary by child; the device is a tool for consistent practice, not a guarantee of independent behavior.'
  ]},
  {title:'Why the restricted digital environment matters', paragraphs:[
    'Goally says its dedicated tablets do not offer a general web browser, YouTube, social media or advertising. Its curated environment is a meaningful distinction from a general-purpose tablet, where families need to configure content and app restrictions.',
    'Apple offers substantial parental controls, and a well-configured iPad can be an excellent learning device. Goally’s advantage is that its narrow purpose is built into the product from the start. No connected device eliminates every risk, and active parental involvement remains important.'
  ]},
  {title:'Practical life skills deserve a place alongside academics', paragraphs:[
    'Reading, writing and counting matter enormously. So do washing hands, tidying toys, communicating needs and navigating a morning routine. Goally’s video classes and daily-skills activities emphasize these real-world lessons.',
    'What makes this approach appealing is the connection between practice on a device and participation in family life. The most valuable moment may come after the screen is put down, when a child tries a newly practiced skill for themselves.'
  ]},
  {title:'Emotional awareness is part of learning', paragraphs:[
    'Young children are still learning to identify feelings, handle transitions and recover from frustration. Goally offers activities such as Mood Tuner and calming content intended to support emotional awareness and regulation.',
    'These features work best as conversation starters: a parent can help a child name a feeling and practice a calming response. They are not treatment, and they should not be represented as proven to prevent meltdowns or replace professional support.'
  ]},
  {title:'Early academic learning without losing the bigger picture', paragraphs:[
    'Goally lists familiar educational options including Khan Academy Kids, PBS Kids and Moose Math. Children can practice foundational academic concepts alongside routines and practical activities.',
    'The combination is appealing for families who want a first learning tablet to support both school readiness and daily independence. Check the manufacturer’s current app list before purchase, because availability and included services can change.'
  ]},
  {title:'Designed for different ways of learning', paragraphs:[
    'Some children respond best to spoken instructions. Others prefer pictures, predictable sequences, repeated demonstrations or a timer. Goally gives parents multiple ways to present a task, making it potentially useful for children who benefit from structure.',
    'Families supporting children with ADHD, autism or communication differences may find these features worth discussing with their child’s educators or clinicians. Individual needs differ, and Goally is not a substitute for personalized care or evidence-based intervention.'
  ]},
  {title:'Rewards can celebrate effort without taking over', paragraphs:[
    'Goally allows parents to connect points and rewards to routines and responsibilities. A child might earn a chance to choose a story or a family activity after completing a manageable goal.',
    'We prefer using rewards to recognize progress and gradually build intrinsic motivation, rather than making every task a transaction. Parents can adjust expectations as their child becomes more confident.'
  ]}
];
const scores = [
